  "components.beta24.help.httpsPrepare": "Prepare HTTPS for the hostname or IP address used on your phone. Download the public bionic-autorite.crt authority and compare its full SHA-256 fingerprint with the one shown on the PC.",
  "components.beta24.help.httpsInstallAuthority": "Install this authority as a CA certificate in your device’s system settings. Downloading the file alone is not enough. The browser cannot confirm this import for you.",
  "components.beta24.help.httpsVerify": "Open secure verification and confirm only if there is no certificate warning. Then return to the companion’s usual HTTPS address and sign in again. You can then add the app to your home screen from the browser menu if you wish.",
  "components.beta24.help.authorityInstallTitle": "Where should you install the public authority?",
  "components.beta24.help.authorityAndroid": "Android: in security settings, search for Certificate, then Install a certificate → CA certificate. Choose the .crt, not a Wi-Fi certificate. Labels vary by manufacturer.",
  "components.beta24.help.authorityIos": "iPhone/iPad: install the downloaded profile in Settings, then enable full trust in General → About → Certificate Trust Settings.",
  "components.beta24.help.authorityWindows": "Windows: in certmgr.msc for the browser’s user account, import the .crt under Trusted Root Certification Authorities → Certificates.",
  "components.beta24.help.certificateWarning": "If a warning appears, note the exact address and NET::ERR_CERT_… code without sharing tickets from a verification URL. Check the correct authority, the covered hostname/IP address and the dates. After a correct import on Android, closing and reopening Chrome, then restarting the phone if needed, is an observed recovery approach; it is not guaranteed to fix every error. Do not bypass the warning.",
